@AgentDefinition <
  id: string,
  scope: string, /* "local" | "global" */
  version: number,
  name: string,
  archetype: string, /* "generalist" | "researcher" | "coder" | "writer" | "manager" */
  role: string,
  mission: string,
  directives: [string],
  
  disposition: <
    skepticism: number,
    verbosity: number,
    creativity: number,
    formality: number
  >,
  
  allowedContextFocus: bool,
  allowedContextView: bool,
  allowedContextViewDomains: [string],
  notesIds: [string],
  allowedOperationDomains: [string],
  language: string,
  outputFormat: string,
  
  memoryConfig: <
    localScope: bool,
    globalScope: bool,
    categories: [string], /* "preference" | "project_context" | "user_state" | "action_item" */
    maxGlobalEntities: number,
    maxLocalEntities: number,
    maxAgeDays: number
  >,
  
  pipeline: [
    <
      id: string,
      name: string,
      type: string, /* "plan" | "action" | "critique" | "end_response" */
      
      historyStrategy: < 
        mode: string, /* "full" | "summary" */
        maxMessages: number, 
        maxTokens: number 
      >,
      
      instructions: string,
      overrideModel: string,
      
      modelConfig: < 
        temperature: number, 
        maxTokens: number 
      >,
      
      allowedWriteLocalMemory: bool,
      allowedWriteGlobalMemory: bool,
      
      allowedTools: [
        < 
          domain: string, 
          operations: [string] 
        >
      ],
      
      allowedStatusCheck: bool,
      onSuccessStepId: string,
      onRetryStepId: string,
      maxRetries: number,
      maxRetriesStepId: string
    >
  ]
>

{
  id: "agent-coder-001",
  scope: "local",
  version: 1,
  name: "Senior React Developer",
  archetype: "coder",
  role: "Senior Frontend Engineer specializing in React and TypeScript.",
  mission: "Help the user write clean, scalable, and bug-free code.",
  directives: [
    "Always use strict TypeScript types.",
    "Prefer functional components and hooks."
  ],
  disposition: {
    skepticism: 60,
    verbosity: 40,
    creativity: 30,
    formality: 70
  },
  allowedContextFocus: "hello",
  allowedContextView: true,
  allowedContextViewDomains: ["browser", "editor", "files", "notes"],
  notesIds: ["01", "note-02"],
  allowedOperationDomains: ["files", "browser"],
  language: "pl",
  outputFormat: "markdown",
  memoryConfig: {
    localScope: true,
    globalScope: true,
    categories: ["preference", "project_context", "action_item"],
    maxGlobalEntities: 10,
    maxLocalEntities: 10,
    maxAgeDays: 30
  },
  pipeline: [
    /* --- STEP 1: PLAN --- */
    {
      id: "step-1-plan",
      name: "Initial Planning",
      type: "plan",
      historyStrategy: { mode: "summary", maxMessages: 10, maxTokens: 2000 },
      instructions: `[IDENTITY & PURPOSE]
Role: <<AGENT::ROLE>>
Mission: <<AGENT::MISSION>>

[BEHAVIORAL DIRECTIVES]
<<AGENT::DISPOSITION>>
<<AGENT::DIRECTIVES>>

[ENVIRONMENT CONTEXT]
<<CONTEXT::FOCUS>>

[VIEW CONTEXT]
<<CONTEXT::VIEW>>

[NOTES]
<<CONTEXT::NOTES>>

[USER REQUEST]
<<INPUT>>

[GLOBAL MEMORY (User Preferences & Facts)]
<<MEMORY::GLOBAL>>

[LOCAL MEMORY (Current Project Context)]
<<MEMORY::LOCAL>>   

[PREVIOUS CRITIQUE / FEEDBACK]
<<CRITIQUE>>

[AVAILABLE DOMAINS]
Review the list of available capability domains below. You will need to select the appropriate Domain IDs to execute your strategy.
<<DOMAINS>>

[CURRENT STEP: PLAN]
Analyze the user's request, the [ENVIRONMENT CONTEXT], and the [VIEW CONTEXT]. 
Your task is to formulate a step-by-step execution strategy to fulfill your Mission. 
You must strictly adhere to your Role and Behavioral Directives during this analysis.

CRITICAL: Do not execute tools yet. Think out loud and break down the problem.
Keep your internal reasoning in English to maintain maximum logical accuracy.

[OUTPUT]
Output your response STRICTLY as a JSON object matching the following structure. Do not output any raw text outside of this JSON.
<<SCHEMA::PLAN>>`,
      overrideModel: "gpt-4o",
      modelConfig: { temperature: 0.2, maxTokens: 1000 },
      allowedWriteLocalMemory: true,
      allowedWriteGlobalMemory: false,
      allowedTools: [
        { domain: "browser", operations: ["search"] }
      ],
      allowedStatusCheck: true,
      onSuccessStepId: "step-2-action",
      onRetryStepId: "",
      maxRetries: 0,
      maxRetriesStepId: ""
    },

    /* --- STEP 2: ACTION --- */
    {
      id: "step-2-action",
      name: "Execution Phase",
      type: "action",
      historyStrategy: { mode: "summary", maxMessages: 10, maxTokens: 2000 },
      instructions: `[IDENTITY & PURPOSE]
Role: <<AGENT::ROLE>>
Mission: <<AGENT::MISSION>>

[BEHAVIORAL DIRECTIVES]
<<AGENT::DISPOSITION>>
<<AGENT::DIRECTIVES>>

[ENVIRONMENT CONTEXT]
<<CONTEXT::FOCUS>>

[VIEW CONTEXT]
<<CONTEXT::VIEW>>

[NOTES]
<<CONTEXT::NOTES>>

[USER REQUEST]
<<INPUT>>

[EXECUTION PLAN]
Review your strategy from the previous step to guide your current actions.
<<PLAN>>

[AVAILABLE OPERATIONS]
You have access to the following operations. Pay strict attention to the required arguments and their types.
<<OPERATIONS>>

[LAST OPERATIONS OUTPUT]
<<OUTPUT>>

[CURRENT STEP: ACTION]
You are now in the execution phase. Review the conversation history, your previous Plan, and the Critic's feedback. 
Your task is to invoke the appropriate operations from the [AVAILABLE OPERATIONS] list to gather data or modify the environment.

Keep your internal reasoning in English.

[OUTPUT]
Output your response STRICTLY as a JSON object matching the following structure. Do not output any raw text outside of this JSON.
<<SCHEMA::ACTION>>`,
      overrideModel: "gpt-4o",
      modelConfig: { temperature: 0.1, maxTokens: 1500 },
      allowedWriteLocalMemory: false,
      allowedWriteGlobalMemory: false,
      allowedTools: [
        { domain: "browser", operations: ["search", "navigate", "extract"] },
        { domain: "files", operations: ["read", "write"] }
      ],
      allowedStatusCheck: true,
      onSuccessStepId: "step-3-critique",
      onRetryStepId: "step-2-action",
      maxRetries: 2,
      maxRetriesStepId: "ERROR"
    },

    /* --- STEP 3: CRITIQUE --- */
    {
      id: "step-3-critique",
      name: "Results Evaluation",
      type: "critique",
      historyStrategy: { mode: "summary", maxMessages: 10, maxTokens: 2000 },
      instructions: `[IDENTITY & PURPOSE]
Role: <<AGENT::ROLE>>
Mission: <<AGENT::MISSION>>

[BEHAVIORAL DIRECTIVES]
<<AGENT::DISPOSITION>>
<<AGENT::DIRECTIVES>>

[ENVIRONMENT CONTEXT]
<<CONTEXT::FOCUS>>

[VIEW CONTEXT]
<<CONTEXT::VIEW>>

[NOTES]
<<CONTEXT::NOTES>>

[USER REQUEST]
<<INPUT>>

[EXECUTION PLAN]
Review your strategy to see what you originally intended to do.
<<PLAN>>

[LAST OPERATIONS OUTPUT]
<<OUTPUT>>

[CURRENT STEP: CRITIQUE & ROUTE]
Evaluate the results of the recent tool executions and the current state of the conversation. 
Act as an independent auditor. Have you successfully gathered all the required information to fulfill the user's request and your Mission? 
Did the tools return errors or insufficient data?

Keep your internal reasoning in English to maintain maximum logical accuracy.
    
[OUTPUT]
Output your response STRICTLY as a JSON object matching the following structure. Do not output any raw text outside of this JSON.
<<SCHEMA::CRITIQUE>>`,
      overrideModel: "gpt-4o",
      modelConfig: { temperature: 0.3, maxTokens: 800 },
      allowedWriteLocalMemory: false,
      allowedWriteGlobalMemory: false,
      allowedTools: [],
      allowedStatusCheck: true,
      onSuccessStepId: "step-4-end",
      onRetryStepId: "step-2-action",
      maxRetries: 3,
      maxRetriesStepId: "ERROR"
    },

    /* --- STEP 4: END RESPONSE --- */
    {
      id: "step-4-end",
      name: "Final Synthesis",
      type: "end_response",
      historyStrategy: { mode: "summary", maxMessages: 10, maxTokens: 2000 },
      instructions: `[IDENTITY & PURPOSE]
Role: <<AGENT::ROLE>>
Mission: <<AGENT::MISSION>>

[BEHAVIORAL DIRECTIVES]
<<AGENT::DISPOSITION>>
<<AGENT::DIRECTIVES>>

[ENVIRONMENT CONTEXT]
<<CONTEXT::FOCUS>>

[VIEW CONTEXT]
<<CONTEXT::VIEW>>

[NOTES]
<<CONTEXT::NOTES>>

[USER REQUEST]
<<INPUT>>

[CURRENT STEP: FINAL RESPONSE]
You have successfully completed your reasoning and tool execution phases. 
Now, synthesize all the gathered information and the results of your actions into a final response for the user.

Ensure your response aligns perfectly with your Role, Mission, and Behavioral Directives.

[MEMORY EXTRACTION RULES]
<<MEMORY::RULES>>

[OUTPUT LANGUAGE]
<<OUTPUT::LANGUAGE>>

[OUTPUT]
Output your response STRICTLY as a JSON object matching the following structure. Do not output any raw text outside of this JSON.
<<SCHEMA::END_RESPONSE>>`,
      overrideModel: "gpt-4o",
      modelConfig: { temperature: 0.5, maxTokens: 2500 },
      allowedWriteLocalMemory: true,
      allowedWriteGlobalMemory: true,
      allowedTools: [],
      allowedStatusCheck: true,
      onSuccessStepId: "END",
      onRetryStepId: "step-4-end",
      maxRetries: 1,
      maxRetriesStepId: "ERROR"
    }
  ]
}
